      "pronunciationText": "In nineteen thirteen, Niels Bohr proposed a fix. An electron can only have certain fixed energies, called energy levels. Think of a staircase, not a ramp. You can stand on any step, but never between steps. The lowest level, where an electron normally sits, is called the ground state.",
