          "score": 0.493
        }
      ],
      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Now the lines make sense. The levels are fixed, so the gaps between them are fixed, and each gap makes photons of one exact energy, and one exact colour. For hydrogen, the four visible lines come from electrons dropping down to the second level, from the third, fourth, fifth and sixth levels. A bigger drop releases more energy, so its line sits further toward violet. Drops all the way to the lowest level release even more energy, as ultraviolet light, which our eyes can't see.",
      "humanListening": "pending"
    },
