      "requestAttempts": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "This is why line spectra are such strong evidence for Bohr's idea. Every element has its own set of energy levels, so it gives out its own pattern of lines, like a fingerprint. Sodium, for example, gives out a strong yellow-orange line. That's the colour you see when a sodium compound is held in a flame, and you'll collect flame colours yourself in a later practical video.",
