      "pronunciationText": "The electron drops, so the atom loses energy, and a photon is emitted. Its energy is the gap: four point one minus one point six, which is two point five times ten to the minus nineteen joules. Adding the two, to get five point seven, is the slip. A photon carries the difference between the levels, not the sum.",
