      "pronunciationText": "Notice how the model of the atom kept changing. The nuclear model couldn't explain line spectra, so Bohr changed it, and Schrödinger changed it again when Bohr's model didn't work for bigger atoms. Each time, new evidence forced a better model. Next time, we'll use that same habit in our own investigations, and see how new evidence can improve a testable chemistry question.",
